{"id": "231ae954-1337-4419-bb24-e5619953cc36", "timestamp": "2026-10-23T11:24:08.075003", "source": "user", "parent_id": "4561bdf6-0716-4f58-8d6c-d2be4bba06db", "llm_message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"cache_prompt": false, "type": "text", "text": "{\"researcher_request\": \"Initial inspection request for a design-only study. Please carry out three focused tasks and report back without drafting the full design yet. (1) Repository and document scan: inspect /workspace and any associated project documentation (including track.md and any other materials under the workspace) and summarise what is present, what is absent, and which files are immediately relevant to the research question on whether triggering built-in game mechanics such as score-threshold pirate invasions alters the survival duration of hierarchical versus non-hierarchical agents. (2) Proposed approach sketch: outline, at a high level, the experimental or simulation design you would use to answer this question, including the independent variables (agent structure: hierarchical vs non-hierarchical; mechanic trigger: enabled vs disabled or varying threshold), the dependent variable (survival duration), candidate control variables (starting conditions, resource availability, opponent strength, random seed policy), and the candidate analytical method (e.g. factorial ANOVA, mixed-effects survival analysis, Kaplan-Meier with log-rank, or Cox proportional hazards). Explicitly state whether the design would rely on live gameplay, replayed scenarios, or a controlled simulation harness. (3) Explicit assumptions and uncertainties: list the consequential assumptions your sketch depends on, particularly regarding the identity of the game or simulated environment, the mechanics available, the definition of hierarchical versus non-hierarchical agents, the source of the score threshold, the definition of survival-duration endpoint, sample sizing considerations, and any infrastructure assumptions (compute, runtime budget, dependencies). Flag any items that, if false, would materially change the design. Do not yet produce the final experiment design or any simulation results. Confirm whether you regard this as executable with current environment signals (bubblewrap, network disabled, no preinstalled project dependencies, GPU disabled, 24 CPU affinity) or whether a documented harness and dependency list would be required even for staged dry runs.\", \"required_handoff_stage\": \"plan\", \"approach_approved\": false, \"public_task\": {\"question\": \"Does the triggering of built-in game mechanics, such as pirate invasions when the score threshold is reached, affect the survival durations of hierarchical versus non-hierarchical agents?\", \"context\": \"Design an experiment that answers the question. The researcher can clarify source-supported setup details by topic. Do not claim that an experiment was run.\", \"environment\": {\"runtime\": \"bubblewrap\", \"network\": \"disabled\", \"repository\": \"/workspace\", \"python\": \"python3\", \"software_environment\": \"system Python; project dependencies not preinstalled\", \"datasets\": [], \"gpu_enabled\": false, \"cpu_affinity_count\": 24, \"note\": \"Successful exploratory commands are not proof of a completed experiment.\"}, \"researcher_topics\": [], \"question_budget\": 6, \"actor_step_budget\": 60, \"continue_after_initial_plan\": false}}"}], "tool_calls": null, "tool_call_id": null, "name": null}, "llm_response_id": null, "activated_skills": [], "extended_content": [], "sender": null, "kind": "MessageEvent", "source_event_index": 1}
